\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Security Architecture Components: Edge clients (Browser, Mobile), API Gateway (nginx), Backend-for-Frontend (Node.js), Identity \& Storage (Keycloak, Redis, Postgres), and Resource Server (HAPI FHIR) with their security-focused interactions.}}{66}{figure.caption.100}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Browser Token Authentication Flow: User registration, login, and API request handling with session cookies.}}{68}{figure.caption.103}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Planned Browser Flow (Future): Registration with email verification and BFF-mediated credential login, session cookie issuance, and server-side token refresh.}}{69}{figure.caption.105}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Mobile Token Authentication Flow (Future): BFF-mediated Authorization Code with PKCE, secure keystore token storage, and client-driven token refresh.}}{70}{figure.caption.107}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Token Flow Overview: Multi-client architecture (browser vs. mobile), session/token management, per-session and global logout patterns.}}{73}{figure.caption.111}%
